# CMake library targets may omit public headers and consumer compile definitions.
id:                     E7008-draft-A7F3
trigger_tool:           conan-create|cmake|cmake-install|consumer-build
phase:                  recipe-design|package|test-package
error_signature:        'consumer.*header.*not found|undefined reference.*public API|public API.*not declared|installed package.*include.*empty'
severity:               2
category:               packaging|cmake|consumer|headers|compile-definitions
match_keywords:         CMake library target, missing installed headers, public header staging, consumer compile definition, Conan cpp_info defines
root_cause:             An upstream CMake project can build a library target successfully while its install rules omit public headers.  Public declarations can also be conditional on a producer-side macro, so a consumer compiles or links incorrectly unless the recipe stages the headers and exports the required definition.
affected_scope:         CMake-based C/C++ libraries whose upstream install() rules cover only the binary target or whose public headers use feature/API guard macros.
verification_cmd:       configure and build the library; inspect the staged package include/lib files; build a separate consumer through generated CMake package metadata; run the consumer against a real API call
rec_priority:            1
rec_approach:           inspect-install-and-public-api
rec_description:        Read the upstream install rules and public header guards before writing package_info.  If headers are absent from install(), copy only the documented public headers during package().  If an API guard is required by the library build, export it through cpp_info.defines so generated CMake consumers inherit it.  Validate with a separate linked consumer rather than a file-existence test.
rec_command:            'cmake --install <build>; inspect package include/lib; build and run an API consumer with generated CMakeDeps/CMakeToolchain'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-consumer-guard
fallback_description:   When automatic public-header discovery is unavailable, list the upstream public headers explicitly and keep the consumer compile definition explicit in the recipe and test target.
fallback_command:       'copy verified public headers; export the required definition; compile and execute one real API path'
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          packaging
forbid_1_pattern:        package.*all.*header
forbid_1_reason:         Copying every source header can expose private implementation details and unstable internals.
forbid_1_consequence:   Consumers may depend on unsupported internals and the package ABI surface becomes unreviewable.
forbid_2_pattern:        test.*print.*version|test.*file.*exists
forbid_2_reason:         Metadata or file-presence checks do not prove that the exported target links and executes the public API.
forbid_2_consequence:   A broken include path, compile definition, or link interface can pass the false test.
principles:              P003, P007, P018
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
